<title>FINLAND: AKTIA CUTS FINNISH 1997, 1998 JOBLESS RATE FCASTS.</title>
<headline>AKTIA CUTS FINNISH 1997, 1998 JOBLESS RATE FCASTS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish Aktia Bank said on</p>
<p>Wednesday it had cut its Finnish unemployment rate forecasts for</p>
<p>the years 1997 and 1998 to 14.4 and 13.3 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Its previous 1997 jobless rate forecast was 15.5 percent and</p>
<p>the 1998 forecast was 14.6 percent.</p>
<p>All its other forecasts for the Finnish economy were</p>
<p>unchanged. It gave the follwing figures (percentage change</p>
<p>unless stated):</p>
<p>			  1997	  1998</p>
<p> GDP			+4	  +3.5</p>
<p> Exports		  +7	    +5</p>
<p> Imports		  +6	    +7</p>
<p> Cons/pr iv	     +4	    +4</p>
<p> Investment	     +5	    +7</p>
<p> C/A (bln)	     +18	   +15</p>
<p> CPI		    +1.5	  +2.5</p>
<p> Jobless (percent)  14.4	  13.3</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
